54
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:26,490
a nearly perfect bell. Here is the surprising

55
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:29,230
part. Start with a lopsided die. One that

56
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:31,600
lands on six half the time. Add enough

57
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,460
of them together and the lopsidedness melts away.

58
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:36,890
You still get the same bell. This is

59
00:02:36,890 --> 00:02:39,840
called the central limit theorem. When you add

60
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:43,190
