71
00:03:10,650 --> 00:03:13,260
what is the exact shape of this curve?

72
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:16,370
The answer comes from a surprising place. Imagine

73
00:03:16,370 --> 00:03:18,910
throwing darts at a target. Your hand is

74
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:22,530
not perfect. Now assume just two things. First,

75
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:25,070
your mistake left or right has nothing to

76
00:03:25,070 --> 00:03:27,780
do with your mistake up or down. Second,

77
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:30,330
only the distance from the center matters. Not

78
00:03:30,330 --> 00:03:33,491
the direction. Those two simple rules force a

79
00:03:33,490 --> 00:03:36,170
single answer. The chance of missing by a

80
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:38,340
